cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use any Trinity S³AI research findings, please cite our complete scientific collection. This work represents defensive publication of 40+ innovations across ternary computing, FPGA architecture, neural networks, and autonomous orchestration."
title: "Trinity S³AI Framework — Complete Scientific Collection v5.2"
abstract: "Trinity S³AI (Sacred Symbolic AI) Framework presents a comprehensive approach to ternary computing with 40+ documented innovations across 7 research domains: (1) Ternary Neural Networks — HSLM-1.95M achieves PPL 125.3 on TinyStories with 20× memory compression; (2) Zero-DSP FPGA — Pure LUT-based inference requiring 0 DSP blocks with 37.8% LUT reduction; (3) TRI-27 ISA — 27-register balanced ternary instruction set with Coptic 3-bank encoding; (4) Queen Lotus Cycle — 6-phase autonomous orchestration with Jaccard similarity retrieval; (5) Tri Language — Linear types, algebraic effects, dual-target codegen to Zig/Verilog; (6) Sacred GF16/TF3 — φ-optimal number formats with 98.4% information retention; (7) VSA Operations — HybridBigInt SIMD achieving 17.2× speedup. All implementations are pure Zig 0.15.x with zero external dependencies, complete reproducibility artifacts, and MLSys reproducibility cards."
